<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n26660" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">līmōsus</span></b> , a, um,
			adj.
		2. limus, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>full of mud</i> or <i>slime, slimy,
				miry, muddy</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quae (aqua) flumine Nilo fertur, adeo est
					limosa atque turbida, etc.,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hirt. B. Alex. 5</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">limosoque palus obducit pascua junco,</span>”
				i. e. <i>growing in muddy places</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					E. 1, 49</span></i>
			; cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">radix,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					27, 1, 17, § 34</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lacus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 2, 135</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ripae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					Am. 3, 6, 1</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">harena,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Tr. 4, 1, 7</span></i>
			.—<i>Plur. absol.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">līmōsa</span></b> ,
				ōrum, n., <i>muddy</i> or <i>miry places</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 9, 42,
				66, § 142</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
